    "result_text": "There's a single test class, and the full build passes. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line now also logs `membershipLevel` (already present) and `membershipNumber`, with all prior fields retained.\n\nChanges:\n- **New `util/MembershipNumberFormatter.java`** \u2014 extracted the membership-number derivation (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`, null when either input is absent) into a small single-responsibility util, mirroring the existing `MembershipLevelCalculator`.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `formatMembershipNumber` now delegates to the new util instead of holding the logic inline, so the format lives in one place.\n- **`rest/OwnerAuditLogger.ownerCreated`** \u2014 appended `membershipNumber={}` to the AUDIT line, sourcing the value from the shared `MembershipNumberFormatter` (reusing, not copying).\n\nBuild is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`), and the audit line now emits e.g. `... membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26`.",
